  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently when uploading an avatar you see your avatar either in the bicycle pose or something put in the animator.\nHowever it would be nice to be able to provide details on how the thumbnail is captured by supplying a pose/animation and a camera position (with settings)\nIn the avatar descriptor adding a section called \"Upload\" or \"Thumbnail\" could include an animation and a reference to a camera object present in the scene.\nThis camera's settings (FOV/Clipping/background etc) are then used when the upload initiates.",
